problem: Create a standalone PR for a local fuse mount fix without mixing it into the hardware-key branch
approach: Stashed the dirty fuse.rs change, branched from main, restored only that file, extracted a tiny auto-unmount policy helper for testability, and validated both default and fuse-feature test paths
failed_paths:
  - Initial gh pr create raced with push because parallel bash ops do not serialize
verification:
  - cargo fmt --all --check
  - cargo test
  - cargo test --features fuse auto_unmount
  - git rev-list --left-right --count origin/main...HEAD
workflow_learning: When using batch bash ops for ship steps, combine dependent git/gh commands in one shell command or run them sequentially
related_files:
  - src/commands/fuse.rs
